#. Tag: title
#: headerfooter.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With multi-page documents, you might want to provide certain information at "
"the top or bottom of each page throughout the document. Headers or footers "
"can provide the reader with important information and they tie your "
"documents together visually."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Headers and footers are special frames. You can edit the text and data "
"within the headers and footers just as you would any other text frame. What "
"makes headers and footers different from most other frames in &kword; is "
"that they are automatically created at the top and bottom of each page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Headers and footers are only available when using text oriented templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: headerfooter.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using headers and footers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can toggle headers and footers on and off independently at any time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can toggle the headers by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable/Disable Document Headers</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can toggle the footers by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable/Disable Document Footers</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The footers will be added below the margins you set under page setup. The "
"text within the main frames will be moved so the headers and/or footers do "
"not overlap any text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since headers and footers are simply text frames that are placed on each "
"page, you can use all of the tools and techniques you are familiar with to "
"create your header and footer information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on options for headers and footers, see the section on "
"<link linkend=\"page-format\">Formatting the page</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information on page numbers see the section on <link linkend=\"page-"
"number\">Page Numbering</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information on formatting the frame, see the section on <link linkend="
"\"format-frame\">Setting the Properties for a Frame</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: headerfooter.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For an example of how to place the page numbers on the outside of even and "
"odd pages, see the <link linkend=\"qd-page-numbers\">How do I?</link> "
"section."
msgstr ""
